    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26220" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lēnīmentum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				softening</i> or <i>soothing remedy; an
				alleviation, mollification</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 25, 5,
				24, § 59</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">addito honestae missionis lenimento,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					2, 67</span></i>
			.</div>
